WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.769
Coding Exercise 2 changes the population rule This
time every

00:00:05.782 --> 00:00:11.140
patient must appear even when no admission exists
That phrase every patient

00:00:11.166 --> 00:00:16.511
tells you which side must be preserved The SELECT
list is already

00:00:16.537 --> 00:00:22.768
started Complete the join between patients and
admissions Before

00:00:22.795 --> 00:00:27.218
running it predict what the unmatched patient row
should look like The

00:00:27.245 --> 00:00:30.902
patient ID and name should still have values while
admission ID and

00:00:30.929 --> 00:00:36.368
diagnosis should be NULL After you select Run and
Check scan the

00:00:36.394 --> 00:00:41.792
output for that unmatched patient Also notice that
patients with multiple admissions

00:00:41.818 --> 00:00:46.896
still create multiple rows The goal is to connect
the wording of

00:00:46.922 --> 00:00:51.214
the requirement with the join type Do not choose
LEFT JOIN only

00:00:51.227 --> 00:00:55.688
because this is a LEFT JOIN exercise Choose it
because the patient

00:00:55.714 --> 00:00:57.714
population must remain complete
